      "raw_response": "Claim: Citrullinated proteins externalized in neutrophil extracellular traps act indirectly to perpetuate the inflammatory cycle via induction of autoantibodies.\n\nThe abstract directly supports the claim. It states that RA neutrophils externalized citrullinated autoantigens during NETosis and that this process correlates with ACPA presence and levels, as well as with systemic inflammatory markers. Furthermore, it shows that autoantibodies to citrullinated proteins can significantly enhance NETosis. Additionally, the inflammatory cytokines IL-17A and TNF-\u03b1 can induce NETosis in RA neutrophils, and NETs can significantly augment inflammatory responses in RA and OA synovial fibroblasts. These findings imply that the externalization of citrullinated autoantigens and immunostimulatory molecules in NETs promotes inflammation, which supports the claim that citrullinated proteins in NETs contribute to perpetuating the inflammatory cycle through autoantibody induction.\n\nANSWER: SUPPORTED",
